<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>b_beam</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.6">model.sdf</sdf>
  <description>
    Wide-pad dogbone beam course: a 3 ft x 2 m start pad, a 6 ft 8 in long x
    12 cm wide beam, and a 3 ft x 2 m end pad, all 1 cm thick with open air either
    side of the beam.  Start pad is centred on the map origin and the beam runs
    along +x with its centreline on y=0.

    meshes/b_beam.{stl,ply} hold the same geometry in map coordinates, so the
    world include uses an identity pose.  The .ply is what
    mesh_to_grid_map_node loads to build the terrain map, and it is read raw
    into the map frame -- the world pose is not applied to it, so the two must
    stay in the same frame.
  </description>
</model>
